    fix(lib): fetch_verified fails closed when the destination cannot be created (CF-280)
    
    scripts/lib.sh fetch_verified() checked the download and the digest, then ran
    
      mkdir -p "$(dirname "$dest")"
      mv "$tmp" "$dest"
      chmod +x "$dest" 2>/dev/null || true
    
    with no status check on either step, so the function's exit status was the last
    command's — the `chmod ... || true` — which is 0 even when mkdir -p or mv failed.
    Callers branch on that status (scripts/install-go.sh:139 `if ! fetch_verified ...
    ; then bad "go:download" ...; exit 1; fi`), so a failed install was recorded as a
    successful, digest-verified install.
    
    The fix checks each step that places the artifact:
    
      1. local dir="$(dirname "$dest")"; `mkdir -p "$dir"` is checked. On failure:
         rm -f "$tmp", a named reason on stderr naming the directory and the url,
         return 1.
      2. `mv "$tmp" "$dest"` is checked. On failure: rm -f "$tmp", a named reason on
         stderr naming the destination and the url, return 1.
      3. `chmod +x "$dest" 2>/dev/null || true` stays best-effort and only runs once
         the file is actually in place; the function then `return 0` explicitly, so no
         trailing `|| true` decides its status. No `set -e` is introduced — lib.sh is
         sourced by many scripts, so every check is explicit. The signature, the
         digest-mismatch stderr message and the tmp-file cleanup are unchanged.
    
    tests/selftest.sh section 5 ("fetch_verified refuses a wrong digest") keeps its
    header and its existing two arms untouched, and appends two arms:
    
      arm (a) positive — destination "$tmpd/blocker/bin" whose parent is a regular
        FILE, so mkdir -p fails with ENOTDIR for root and non-root alike (0555 is
        deliberately not used: root ignores it). Asserts a NON-ZERO return AND that no
        artifact was installed at the destination.
      arm (b) caller — a fixture caller written into "$tmpd" that sources
        "$HERE/scripts/lib.sh" and uses the install-go.sh branch shape
        (`fetch_verified ... || { bad "go:download" ...; exit 1; }`). Asserts the
        caller exits non-zero AND that its output carries exactly one row matching
        `^  FAIL  go:download` — the ROW, not the substring FAIL, because a shell
        death also prints FAIL and would fake a pass. `bad` returns its own printf's
        status, so the fixture states `exit 1` instead of inheriting that 0.
    
    A comment above the new arms states the red-proof obligation: reverting the lib.sh
    fix makes both arms fail.
    
    Red-proof (PERFORMED, in copies under /tmp, the real tree untouched): the pre-fix
    body was restored as /tmp/cf280-lib-old.sh and driven by /tmp/cf280-red-proof.sh,
    mirroring both new arms against it:
    
      armA_exit=0 armA_artifact=absent    <- old body reports a verified install
      armB_exit=0 armB_rows=0             <- old body surfaces nothing
      armA_fixed_exit=1                   <- fixed body fails closed
    
    So both new arms are RED under the pre-fix code: regression arms, not decoration.
    
    Measured at this commit:
      bash -n scripts/lib.sh            rc=0
      bash -n tests/selftest.sh         rc=0
      bash tests/selftest.sh > /tmp/cf280-selftest.log 2>&1   rc=0
      summary line                      SELFTEST: PASS
      rows in that log                  363 `  PASS  ` / 58 `  FAIL  `; the 58 FAIL
        rows are the battery's own negative fixtures and are unchanged — the
        pre-change run at b9fa54c-equivalent tree (/tmp/cf280-baseline2.log) printed
        361 PASS / 58 FAIL / SELFTEST: PASS, so the delta is exactly the new rows:
        grep -c '^  PASS  uncreatable destination -> fetch_verified exit 1, no artifact installed$' -> 1
        grep -c "^  PASS  caller surfaced the failed install: 1 '\^  FAIL  go:download' row, fixture exit 1$" -> 1
      note                             the suite's very first run in this session
        printed SELFTEST: FAIL (1) on the pre-existing `section-mapping-real` arm
        (cwd-relative plan/selftest paths); the rerun on the unchanged tree printed
        SELFTEST: PASS and the post-fix run above is green. That flake predates this
        change and is not touched here.
    
    Not done deliberately: no push, no gitreins task/judge run, no board row, no edit
    outside scripts/lib.sh and tests/selftest.sh, no new repo file, and the section-5
    header plus the existing two arms were not renumbered or rewritten.
    
